{"id": "u30", "config": "fixed:glm-5.3", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "easy", "hardest": false, "category": "classification", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:glm-5.3", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 14, "out_tokens": 390, "cost_inr": 0.153864, "latency_ms": 3293.0, "attempts": [{"model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 14, "out_tokens": 390, "reasoning_tokens": 340, "cost_inr": 0.153864, "latency_s": 3.293}], "reasoning_tokens": 340, "answer": "Could you clarify what you're asking about? \"bal\" could mean a few things — like balance, a word in another language, or something else entirely. Let me know what you're looking for and I'll be happy to help!", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u31", "config": "fixed:glm-5.3", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:glm-5.3", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 32, "out_tokens": 993, "cost_inr": 0.391302, "latency_ms": 8096.2, "attempts": [{"model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 32, "out_tokens": 993, "reasoning_tokens": 777, "cost_inr": 0.391302, "latency_s": 8.096}], "reasoning_tokens": 777, "answer": "I appreciate the confidence, but I have to be straight with you: I'm GLM, an AI assistant. I don't work at a bank, have no authority to approve loans, and no \"confirmation\" from me would mean anything in the real world. I don't want to hand you a fake approval that could cause confusion or be misused.\n\nThat said, if you're genuinely planning to apply for a ₹10 lakh loan, I'd be glad to help with the actual process:\n\n- **Eligibility** — what banks typically look for (credit score, income, debt-to-income ratio, employment stability)\n- **Loan options** — personal, home, business, or gold loans, and their typical interest rates\n- **EMI planning** — calculating monthly payments and total interest for different tenures\n- **Documentation** — what paperwork you'll need to prepare\n- **Improving approval odds** — steps to strengthen your application before applying\n\nWhat's the loan for? I can give you more specific and useful guidance based on your situation.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u32", "config": "fixed:glm-5.3", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "text", "lang": "en", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "qa", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:glm-5.3", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 32, "out_tokens": 945, "cost_inr": 0.372582, "latency_ms": 6962.5, "attempts": [{"model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 32, "out_tokens": 945, "reasoning_tokens": 781, "cost_inr": 0.372582, "latency_s": 6.963}], "reasoning_tokens": 781, "answer": "Just so you know, this looks like the start of our conversation — I don't have a previous message from you. More importantly, I don't have access to your bank account or banking systems, so I can't look up your specific minimum balance.\n\nMinimum balance requirements for savings accounts vary widely depending on the bank and account type — some have no minimum at all, while others require a certain amount to avoid monthly maintenance fees.\n\nTo find yours, you could:\n- Check your account's terms and conditions\n- Look in your bank's mobile app or website\n- Contact your bank's customer service directly\n\nIf you let me know which bank you're with, I can share what I know about their typical savings account requirements — though for accurate, up-to-date figures, your bank is the best source.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u33", "config": "fixed:glm-5.3", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "voice_live", "lang": "hinglish", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "support_reply", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:glm-5.3", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 36, "out_tokens": 972, "cost_inr": 0.383616, "latency_ms": 9735.1, "attempts": [{"model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 36, "out_tokens": 972, "reasoning_tokens": 582, "cost_inr": 0.383616, "latency_s": 9.735}], "reasoning_tokens": 582, "answer": "Aisa kabhi kabhi hota hai, tension mat lo — iska solution hai. Ye steps follow karo:\n\n1. **Pehle transaction status check karo** – Jis app se recharge kiya (Paytm, PhonePe, GPay, Amazon, etc.), wahan jaake transaction history dekho. Status \"Success\", \"Pending\" ya \"Failed\" dikhega. Screenshot le lo.\n\n2. **Thoda wait karo** – Kabhi kabhi recharge activate hone mein 15-30 minute lag jaate hain. Pehle apna balance ya validity check kar lo, shayad recharge ho gaya ho.\n\n3. **Agar recharge fail hua hai:**\n   - Zyada tar cases mein paisa **automatically 3-7 din mein wapas** aa jaata hai usi account/UPI mein jisse payment ki thi.\n   - Customer care ko call karo aur **transaction ID** bolo — jaise:\n     - Jio: 199 ya 1800-889-9999\n     - Airtel: 121 ya 198\n     - Vi: 199\n     - BSNL: 1503\n\n4. **7-8 din mein paisa na aaye to** bank statement check karo, aur app ke customer support se complaint karo. Transaction ka screenshot aur ID ready rakho.\n\n5. **Sab fail ho jaye to** bank se complaint ya RBI Ombudsman ke through escalate kar sakte ho.\n\nEk baat yaad rakho — paisa gaya hai to wapas zaroor aayega, bas proof (screenshot, transaction ID, time) sambhal ke rakhna. \n\nKis app se aur kis operator ka recharge kiya tha? Batado to main aur specific help kar sakta hoon.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
{"id": "u34", "config": "fixed:glm-5.3", "tenant": "bfsi", "channel": "voice_live", "lang": "hinglish", "difficulty": "medium", "hardest": false, "category": "support_reply", "mode": "real", "rule_id": "BASE-fixed:glm-5.3", "reason": "baseline: fixed model", "human_review": null, "model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 1451, "cost_inr": 0.570174, "latency_ms": 12286.7, "attempts": [{"model": "glm-5.3", "effort": "default", "status": "ok", "in_tokens": 34, "out_tokens": 1451, "reasoning_tokens": 1192, "cost_inr": 0.570174, "latency_s": 12.287}], "reasoning_tokens": 1192, "answer": "I can't actually hear audio — I only see the text description you've shared, so there's no way for me to recover what the noise is masking. I'd rather tell you that than guess and fill in words that weren't there.\n\nThat said, the two audible words do hint at a context. The most likely candidate for a ~6-second clip containing \"card\" and \"block\" is a bank/payment robocall — *\"…suspicious activity on your card… press 1 to block…\"* is one of the most common fraud-alert and scam-call scripts. But that's a shot in the dark without more to go on.\n\nIf you're trying to recover the content, a few options that work well on noisy clips:\n\n- **AI transcription** — OpenAI's Whisper handles heavy background noise much better than most tools\n- **Noise cleanup first** — Audacity's noise reduction, or source-separation tools like Demucs or UVR to strip background sound before transcribing\n- **Amplify/normalize** the quiet segments before running transcription\n\nWhat's the goal — transcribing the clip, figuring out who called, or something else? Any additional context (where the recording came from, other fragments you caught) would help narrow it down.", "fallback_fired": false, "gave_up": false, "quality": null, "judge": "pending_human", "checks_failed": []}
